:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T15:54:50-07:00","id":1521293,"title":"","content":"Weasel was one of my favorite reads of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T22:49:10-07:00","id":1521316,"title":"","content":"Any ideas about I:cons of Rage release?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T11:00:11-07:00","id":1521341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1521316#post1521316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas about I:cons of Rage release?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s in Art Direction per the last Release Roundup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T06:37:09-07:00","id":1521504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1519142#post1519142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Spirits of the Wolf Slayers of the Impergium - and their tools<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> well, I'm a prophet.<br /> Joke aside, a year and a half ago, I GMed a Werewolf dark age campaign centered around the investigation of a destroyed caern which held chained an old spirit.<br /> <br /> That spirit, the &quot;Silvered Hatred&quot; was the incarnation of the growing hatred of humanity for garou during the impergium (and possibly, a sort of human ancestor spirit of the first to rise against the impergium with silver), until it led humans against them.<br /> <br /> needless to say, it became the main antagonist, making everyday humans a hasard, since it's influence turned the fear caused by the delirium into uncontrollable murder urge toward garou","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T07:31:02-07:00","id":1521509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1521504#post1521504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> well, I'm a prophet.<br /> Joke aside, a year and a half ago, I GMed a Werewolf dark age campaign centered around the investigation of a destroyed caern which held chained an old spirit.<br /> <br /> That spirit, the &quot;Silvered Hatred&quot; was the incarnation of the growing hatred of humanity for garou during the impergium (and possibly, a sort of human ancestor spirit of the first to rise against the impergium with silver), until it led humans against them.<br /> <br /> needless to say, it became the main antagonist, making everyday humans a hasard, since it's influence turned the fear caused by the delirium into uncontrollable murder urge toward garou</div> </div> </div> </div>That is pretty cool. I'm not surprised this idea popped up before, and it wasn't fleshed out a lot here, but it would be cool to play up. Any specific details you went into and how they functioned narratively?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T09:41:07-07:00","id":1521512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1521509#post1521509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is pretty cool. I'm not surprised this idea popped up before, and it wasn't fleshed out a lot here, but it would be cool to play up. Any specific details you went into and how they functioned narratively?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For a bit of context, the campaign was set in the 12th century in Aquitaine (south west of modern day France).<br /> The three PCs were sent in a quest to investigate the recent disappearance of some lone urban garou.<br /> <br /> They found a cell of what they assumed were inquisitors with some rather impressive resistance to gifts and even garou claws. After dispatching them, they found an artifact marked with garou glyphs.<br /> <br /> After following the trace of the artifact, they arived in an abandonned caern in the ardenian forests. Corrupted garou had attacked the caern in order to free the spirit the caern was built to contain.<br /> <br /> And yet the spirit apparently murdered it's would be liberators alongside it's jailors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bFollowing that event, the campaign turned more and more dangerous. Each session was about a small mission, or errant, either choosed by the players or proposed by me as their caern's elders demanding something.<br /> but these apparent side quest were excuses for me to instore a growing sense of hostility toward the PCs. People were reacting in a manner similar to the Curse, but with agressivity rather than unnease. News of nobles rewarding the hunting down of wolves multiplied, and the caern received more and more stories of inquisitors identifying garou and kinfolks with strange ease.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, the spirit revealed itself when the group's theurge lend the pack following a vision of a teenager, in a primitive tent, with blooded hands and tears.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They met it in the umbra, in a small realm reminiscent of a prehistorical village, whose walls were lined with wolves' corpses.<br /> The spirit, appearing as the bloodied adolescent of the theurge's vision, presented itself as Silvered Hatred, the incarnation of the human backlash against the impergium.<br /> <br /> As a character, I played him as a particularly driven human, rather than the way I typically portray spirits, capable of rational discussions, but ultimately, hellbent on exterminating all garou.<br /> <br /> He was also partial on garou depending on their tribes, remembering that the ancestors of the warden of men and children of gaia were against the impergium. Not that it would do them any good, since their only reward would be a quick end, while the spirit desired to hunt down the other till, hiding cowardly from their new hunters, the garou lived what humans lived during the impergium.<br /> <br /> And you don't want to know what he planned with the red talons.<br /> <br /> After escaping the realm, the campaign became pretty much a story of survival. The influence of Silvered Hatred spread pretty much naturally amongs humans thanks to it's chosen ones, the &quot;avengers&quot;, humans who suffered at the hands of garou, and who became easy receptacles of the will of Silvered Hatred.<br /> <br /> In terms of mechanics, in all cities the avengers went, I turned all delirium reactions of fear to pulsion of violence toward garous. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the end, after losing their own caern in a tragic battle against an army assembled by the avenged, the PCs ran away, persuaded that there was no hope. Until they found Sister Hepatia, an ananasi, who, tbey would find out, was the one who tricked the corrupted garou into freeing Silvered Hatred.<br /> <br /> Sister Hepatia, obeying Ananasa, planned for the extermination of garou.<br /> <br /> Following that, the PCs, after a lot of umbral shenanigans, were able to speak with Ananasa, and after a pretty impressive line of arguments from one of the player, was convinced that even after the extermination of garou, Silvered Hatred, being driven by a millenia of hatred, will never stop, and would inevitably hunt down her children.<br /> <br /> Hence she reveals to them his weakness: if at least one of his receptacles were able to renounciate their desire for vengeance for the garou, he would be massively weakened.<br /> <br /> <br /> So they found one of them, the only one they hoped to convince, since he was someone they met early in the campaign, a farmboy whose sister was murdered by a garou, suspecting she was about to turn fomori.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bShort story short, they (barely) suceeded, and with that break of his concept from one of his own chosen one, Silvered Hatred was weakened enough to be vainquished. But not destroyed, for his existence was dependant on the still existing anger of humans towards garou, even if for most humans, that anger was unconscious.<br /> <br /> So the pack trapped Silvered Hatred, and like the founders of the lost caern, dedicated themselves to keeping him emprisonned.<br /> <br /> The campaign ended on a last dialogue between the spirit and the group's theurge. The first taunting the garou that he'll inevitably break free and finish the job, the latter hoping that one day, humanity may forgive the garou, taking away the spirit's nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fun fact, during the campaign, one of the player wondered that, if the hatred of humans during the impergium manifested as a spirit, then the fear of garou caused by said period, and manifesting during the delirium, should also create a spirit.<br /> <br /> And after a discussion on the matter, we agreed that there's indeed such a spirit, but that for garou, it's existence will only ever be theorical, since being born of the fear of garou and being fed by yhe innate delirium of all of mankind, such powerful spirit use it's powers will perpetually avoid meeting them, even in vision or memories, to the point that garou couldn't even see it's trace or even remember other spirits mentioning it. (Yeah, we basically gave it the equivalent of obfuscate 9)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T07:08:01-07:00","id":1521588,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> i love the silver hatred idea and am adopting it into my lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T11:34:55-07:00","id":1521606,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> that's pretty cool as a setup. Hope your players had fun with that.<br /> <br /> Did anyone else get to read Apocalyptic Record? Have any comments on my writeup or things you liked and hated about it?<br /> <br /> I want to writeup the next bit and hoping not to be writing into the void <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 08-29-2023, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T23:23:51-07:00","id":1521649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1521606#post1521606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> that's pretty cool as a setup. Hope your players had fun with that.<br /> <br /> Did anyone else get to read Apocalyptic Record? Have any comments on my writeup or things you liked and hated about it?<br /> <br /> I want to writeup the next bit and hoping not to be writing into the void <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of things I liked in Apocalyptic Record, first the way the stories are told and how it gives us a sense how the WtA setting is changing.<br /> <br /> I think one shining moment was how Blood Red Crest figured that garou born were a way to save their house. Because it made sense in a dark way and unlike the Changing Ways garou born breeding farms, this was one desperate group of garou at their wits end.<br /> <br /> The part that wasn't really my thing was how the BSD redemption was treated as a massive no-go and a fool's errand. Not because I want their redemption to be a common thing, but because it felt like a repeat of the Wyrm20 and Umbra20 where there is a chance ONE BSD might be redeemed, maybe. So the Wretch section and the ST notes on it really didn't add much for me.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the book is solid and its release was overshadowed by W5 in a very bad way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T04:48:18-07:00","id":1521658,"title":"","content":"As one of the contributors, I'm enjoying your summaries and comments. If anyone has further commentary, feedback, or questions, I'm happy to answer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T15:15:26-07:00","id":1521697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1521649#post1521649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the book is solid and its release was overshadowed by W5 in a very bad way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly so, as there's a lot of cool stuff in the Record!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1521658#post1521658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As one of the contributors, I'm enjoying your summaries and comments. If anyone has further commentary, feedback, or questions, I'm happy to answer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for participating! Do you maybe have a favourite section you did in the book ? Or is it in one of the chapters I'm about to go through? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T02:45:25-07:00","id":1521733,"title":"","content":"I'm checking in from time to time! And in terms of Apocalyptic Record being overshadowed by W5, it was a gamble in terms of releasing the books close to each other. I think AR will find its audience though, especially as more people get interested in Werewolf via W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","user":"The Gentleman Gamer","date":". 08-31-2023, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T03:24:06-07:00","id":1521736,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I could pin down a <b>favourite</b> section. But of my own contributions I was extremely pleased to tell the story of Amber Dreaming vs the Australian Garou, simply cuz her introduction in Shattered Dreams was so compressed and I like her role as a Galliard uncovering truths the other Garou seek to ignore, forget, and/or hide.<br /> <br /> Other sections involve Glen Seize-Trouble (not only cuz I &lt;3 puns) as a Ragabash who introduces a Pentex idea I've had since Freak Legion was published. And his tales touch upon a couple of fun (if slightly wild and wacky) theories that I had a lot of fun pondering. Also he's a bit of a fuck up as both a Ragabash and a Stargazer - and suffers for it - albeit his heart is in the right place.<br /> <br /> Jeremiah God-Buyer was probably the most fun to write. Just utter bastardry backed by magic to demonstrate how infuriating it can be to take on a Yeren. Especially on their home turf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T11:35:46-07:00","id":1522172,"title":"","content":"Personally, I consider apocalyptic records to be a disappointment compared to beckett's jyhad diary. For multiple reason.<br /> <br /> One I won't really take account of, since it would be pretty unfair to AR's writters, is that BJD could count on many well known and loved character, while WtA has far less of that. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe bolk covers a lot of ideas, many interesting ones, but there's a few issues<br /> <br /> - First, and for me, the biggest, is the idea of divinding the book by aupices. This to me was a bad idea, because it pushed many disparates ideas into a single chapter, and due to the format, only a few of them are truly develloped into the &quot;here's what you can do with it in game&quot; part at the end of a chapter.<br /> <br /> BJD had a lot of chapters each dedicated to one event/location/concept with the exception of the omega chapter. This allows the &quot;for the ST&quot; part to be more develloped.<br /> <br /> Now look at the last part of AR, the philidox chapter. My personnal favorite. It's chock full of ideas, including the plots of many tribes' fall in the Apocalypse book, or the weird rumors and new ideologies spreading across the younger garous.<br /> <br /> And yet, due to the format of five chapters, all these will barely be mentioned in the &quot;for ST's eyes&quot; part.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bA Division of chapters similar to BJD would have been better. For exemple one chapter about the garouboros and abominations and another on the amazonian war's ending, and another on Bat's redemption.<br /> <br /> Second, many things in the books seems to not really fit in a BJD like book, by that I mean that they don't add anything to what we know of the setting or set up anything for the future.<br /> For exemple the chapter on the captured BSD who ends up not being redemptable. Something that was the status quo since first edition. Or the part where a group of garou has some sort of first contact with a bastet. Which adds up nothing on garou-fera relations that we don't know since feras were introduced.<br /> <br /> these and some others made me feels like the devs knew W20 was coming to an end, they still had some ideas and wanted to implement them in a boof even if that doesn't really match it.<br /> <br /> And that to me is doubly an issue, since the space used for them could have been used to devellop the good new ideas of the book, like the idea of a rise of abominations or explore other mysteries of the setting, like the machine awakening or t he stargazers cosmology.<br /> <br /> Which is sort of a third problem to me. BJD did a stellar job of taking account of most of the main plots and mysteries of VtM. AR seems to miss most of them. From the many exploratory camps and factions (wagnerians, bone gnawers deserters, etc).<br /> <br /> <br /> Fourth one, and that's a personnal peeve, the tbeurge chapter is criminally empty. There's so much mysteries in the umbra that were not taken account of. From the deep umbra, the lost stargazers leaving earth, the search of the wagnerian for another gaia and hell, effing antelios!<br /> <br /> The chapter seems empty compared to, say, the philodox one.<br /> <br /> <br /> And finally, although a little one compared to the other, as a kickstarter participant, I can't help but feel we have had false promises of certain points, notably that we would have the point of views of fera and even wyrm servants.<br /> <br /> Well, we don't have wyrm servants POV, and the ony fera appearing is a bastet that simoky says that the place the narrator's pack is entering in is her territory.<br /> <br /> <br /> So in overall, many good ideas, but a very messy book.<br /> <br /> <br /> Andbon another note, Howls of the apocalypse is truly terrible, but I don't think that's the time and place for speaking of that one.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T12:03:21-07:00","id":1522173,"title":"","content":"The thing is, WtA's metaplot has never been very character-driven. While there certainly are famous NPCs, a lot of the metaplot relies on world events or exposures of unknown lore. WtA's events exist in small pockets while the Kindred generally are very global.<br /> <br /> Plus, there really isn't any need for a historian-type character like Beckett in WtA, since garou already have an auspice to do the job plus access to ancestors. Nor is there really any chance for a character to check out forbidden camps like Beckett is checking forbidden lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T14:03:46-07:00","id":1522179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1522173#post1522173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, WtA's metaplot has never been very character-driven. While there certainly are famous NPCs, a lot of the metaplot relies on world events or exposures of unknown lore. WtA's events exist in small pockets while the Kindred generally are very global.<br /> <br /> Plus, there really isn't any need for a historian-type character like Beckett in WtA, since garou already have an auspice to do the job plus access to ancestors. Nor is there really any chance for a character to check out forbidden camps like Beckett is checking forbidden lore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> this is not a fatality though. Nothin stopped OPP from creating a character, potentially a keeper of the silver record (which is already part of the lore as keepers of global garou knowledge) or, to match with the end of the philodox chapter, a shadow lord spying around in order to give an holistic view of the events across the world to the assembly of shadow lord philodoxes.<br /> <br /> When you look at AR, that's already partly what is tried here, with a narrator gathering lore, if only from secundary sources.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T14:16:45-07:00","id":1522182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1522179#post1522179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is not a fatality though. Nothin stopped OPP from creating a character, potentially a keeper of the silver record (which is already part of the lore as keepers of global garou knowledge) or, to match with the end of the philodox chapter, a shadow lord spying around in order to give an holistic view of the events across the world to the assembly of shadow lord philodoxes.<br /> <br /> When you look at AR, that's already partly what is tried here, with a narrator gathering lore, if only from secundary sources.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how Pattern Recognition and the Geomid Network work, we actually have a convenient set of narrators for the whole thing. I think I would have preferred a thematic linkage instead of an auspice linkage as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T01:52:40-07:00","id":1522207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1522172#post1522172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> these and some others made me feels like the devs knew W20 was coming to an end, they still had some ideas and wanted to implement them in a boof even if that doesn't really match it.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, for what it's worth, the Developers and writers absolutely knew this was the final book ever for W20 (Howls and Icons notwithstanding). This was it, the end.<br /> <br /> So speaking for myself, I tried the best I could to squeeze in the most I could. I'm pretty sure I wasn't alone in that squeezing. That said, time and wordcount are always gonna leave material on the table. I would've loved to include more Fera, or even have a seprate book to cover Fera, but them's the breaks - this was the send off to Werewolf: the Apocalypse, not Fera: the Apocalypse. We had to cover the Garou as the primary focus, being the thing the game was nominally about.<br /> <br /> In some other timeline Paradox would approve a similar book to say goodbye to the Fera, but not this one. (And golly that would be a hard book to do justice to some 15+ Changing Breeds! You could do one per Breed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T17:59:47-07:00","id":1522243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1522207#post1522207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yes, for what it's worth, the Developers and writers absolutely knew this was the final book ever for W20 (Howls and Icons notwithstanding). This was it, the end.<br /> <br /> So speaking for myself, I tried the best I could to squeeze in the most I could. I'm pretty sure I wasn't alone in that squeezing. That said, time and wordcount are always gonna leave material on the table. I would've loved to include more Fera, or even have a seprate book to cover Fera, but them's the breaks - this was the send off to Werewolf: the Apocalypse, not Fera: the Apocalypse. We had to cover the Garou as the primary focus, being the thing the game was nominally about.<br /> <br /> In some other timeline Paradox would approve a similar book to say goodbye to the Fera, but not this one. (And golly that would be a hard book to do justice to some 15+ Changing Breeds! You could do one per Breed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I understand that this is about garou. On that matter, my problem is that, while the part of the book was especially about the relation between fera and garou, she was... Inconsequential to say the least <br /> <br /> On the matter of the war of rage and it's consequences, a nagah, mokole or hell, even an ananasi would have done the job.<br /> <br /> Here we have a bastet that fight garou because they obvioisly wouldn't understand her writte' warning, then speak with them of a rite.<br /> <br /> Not saying this is bad narration, but this would have a place in other books, not the pretty much last book of the whole line dedicated to closing the loops.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, slightly out of topic, but that chapter gave me a litteral sarcastic laughting crisis.<br /> <br /> We have it ladies and gentleman, after around 30 years of WtA, we found it, the first and only living garou who speak in favor of the war of rage!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T00:25:21-07:00","id":1522257,"title":"","content":"yeah, I get it. I would've loved more Fera material too. Wasn't permitted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T01:09:30-07:00","id":1522258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1522257#post1522257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, I get it. I would've loved more Fera material too. Wasn't permitted.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can't be easy writing about aomething you love and then being told you cannot touch X. I do feel that a lot of love went into this. In many ways I would have preferred more freedom for you folks than where we are right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T02:03:09-07:00","id":1522260,"title":"","content":"I mean Apocalyptic Record had a lot of that with Paradox outright forbidding them from cleaning up a bunch of old cobwebs such as Tribe Names etc. but then Paradox did that throughout 20ths run and worse.<br /> <br /> Just wish they would have allowed it for AR especially as W5 is a ' reimagining' and things in AR wouldn't have effected it. But I guess they couldn't take credit for said changes if they'd allowed them to be made by an OPP team.....<br /> <br /> Really sad considering what Leath Sheales wanted to do and wasn't allowed to on the last book before he passed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T03:23:28-07:00","id":1522261,"title":"","content":"Hey there, thanks for the kind words about our book. And the compliments about my sections! (I wrote the Theurge tales about New York, Totems, and all the Bat stuff. And also the metaplot chapter)<br /> <br /> Happy to chime in and say the Morningkill letter in the New York story isn't out of place. It's intentionally there as part of the escalation showing Garou's doing stuff in parallel to Rowena's own journey. When she's at the start, you get the Black Spiral singing about the Wyrm; when she's in the middle, you get Pentex bragging but also saying Garou stopped one of their operations; and when she understood the lessons of the night, you get Isaiah telling about the Garou are about to defeat the Storm Eater by paying high cost for good reasons. Which always was a great example of Garou victory in my mind. And I'm a huge fan of the Werewolf West.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T11:20:14-07:00","id":1522277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1522260#post1522260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean Apocalyptic Record had a lot of that with Paradox outright forbidding them from cleaning up a bunch of old cobwebs such as Tribe Names etc. but then Paradox did that throughout 20ths run and worse.<br /> <br /> Just wish they would have allowed it for AR especially as W5 is a ' reimagining' and things in AR wouldn't have effected it. But I guess they couldn't take credit for said changes if they'd allowed them to be made by an OPP team.....<br /> <br /> Really sad considering what Leath Sheales wanted to do and wasn't allowed to on the last book before he passed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The last book Leath worked on for us was The World Below, and had plenty of creative freedom there. Also his last Werewolf book was Icons of Rage. No need to be sad about his contributions, which were always excellent. We were lucky to have worked with him.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T01:47:14-07:00","id":1522297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1522277#post1522277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The last book Leath worked on for us was The World Below, and had plenty of creative freedom there. Also his last Werewolf book was Icons of Rage. No need to be sad about his contributions, which were always excellent. We were lucky to have worked with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, he did work on Icons. I knew Josh did but didn't know Leath did as well, awesome.<br /> <br /> Haven't checked out The World Below, will do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T13:50:25-07:00","id":1523835,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So, I'm back with Ragabash tales. I kinda bounced hard off the Ragabash chapter and had a problem with working out my thoughts on parts of it in a way that I hope will sound reasonable to folks. For that reason each time I started to write this thing down I ended up not wanting to to engage with what bugged me the most. It was not helped that I managed to lose most of my written summary because I was silly enough to keep it in a browser window instead of elsewhere.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In essence it comes down to the fact that in general I feel that Ragabash are one of the hardest Auspices to play properly in Werewolf. It's easy to interpret them as simply juvenile pranksters or as rote contrarians. But the actual purpose of the Ragabash is to use humor and a skewed perspective to challenge and direct the other Garou. They are there to be scouts, teachers, innovators, challengers and experts at defusing problematic situations. At times too clever for their own good, of course, but the true mark of a Ragabash is being Clever about being Garou and instilling their insights into others.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Which is why reading the Ragabash section left me rather confused and troubled by the perspectives we see. So far the book has presented Garou being dumb in a number of ways and then calling them out for being dumb. The Ragabash chapter has the most spectacular selection of Garou being dumb so far. And yet, there is the least critique of the people who collected this material and a number of behaviours that should at least be criticised, are not.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the Ragabash section we have the following:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Ragabash frenzying while trying to protect his kin, and proceeding to murder all of them indiscriminately</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Ragabash walking into a family gathering, being disgusted by their behavior, leaving and coming back only to murder them all</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Ragabash blowing up a JFK airport terminal with 27 dead casualties (and probably around a hundred wounded)</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The first instance has the Ragabash regretting what they have done and used by John North-Wind's Son to demonstrate the need of thinking and coordinating before acting. Great.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The second instance has the Ragabash acting like a psycho, and there is no punishment nor deeper introspection for them practically excising three generations of their own blood, just because they didn't know better than to be complacent consumerists. Oooook, someone is really keen on hammering the fact that Ragabash too can act on Rage, but the fucker left and came back. That was premeditated murder - of their own family. And is this called out? Is this pointed out that it's a violation of at least two tenets of the Litany? Nope.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The third one has the Ragabash believing they were super smart and efficient at killing a major Wyrm player by bombing a major transportation hub, killing a shitload of innocents and pontificating how they are a weapon, and a weapon must kill. No comment. No critique. No calling out the fact that he cannot even be sure he got the target he was aiming for. What the flying fuck? This goes somewhere along with The Vienna bombing (v5) as a brilliant example of how insane events that would practically cause immense problems not just for the character but in politics and police action are treated over casually causing mass mayhem. And even not dwelling on that, the actions of that character are a horrible example of a Ragabash's job. Again, the author was keen on showing how broken the Garou can be from their war, but forgot to actually point out that this is NOT the way to do things and call them out</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It's bizarre to see that the Ragabash are the worst Garou we are yet to see in the book. And it's even more bizarre that this was something a lot of focus was placed on. I am not sure what was the goal, and the message here? Combined with the fourth crazy Garou in the chapter (who I kinda liked), it's as if I was reading a Twitcher splatbook, not a Ragabash one.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chapter IV - Ragabash Tales\u200b</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The chapter opens with a cool picture of what I assume is a Ragabash on a motorcycle blowing up a Circinus factory. What detracts from it is that they are smoking in front of the Evil Cigarette factory. I guess smoking characters are supposed to be cool in an action scene like this. Still it feels mismatched. What, did the character pick it up in the Factory? Did they have their own collection of cigars just for this opportunity? If it was any other thing being blown up, I wouldn't even have noticed it as much.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stories of Home</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The first tale we encounter is the first incident I outlined above. Pentex is grooming youth to become their new agents by promising them great things and compatriots while giving them superpowers. It's very much Pentex selling fomoridom as gaining X-Men powers <i>(Free-X)</i>. This seems like an interesting antagonist for a specific sort of game, especially the insidious grooming and how deep it can cut into Garou families. I do feel I'd prefer to play down the X Men cues, though. The tale itself is all about how a Ragabash tried to find out what was wrong with his Cousin, and followed up a trail of grooming and systematic co-option only to snap and kill her and her family in a Frenzy.<br /> <br /> The second one is a creepy tale of a Young Persons Care home where the inhabitants were taking part in a ominous &quot;Breeding program&quot;. The whole thing was taken down by cops and there is a lot of uncertain details, but the director implies that they all belong to the &quot;family&quot;. This is framed by a Ragabash that's trying to figure out if the rumors this ties into the Kinfolk is true and could it be tied to the BSD's or the actions of the local Sept. A lot of it is termed in very unclear hearsay and postulation, but I've never been a big fan of the whole idea that a &quot;good&quot; tactic for Garou is to make breeding camps. Considering a lot of allegations what Werewolf is about, maybe a stronger message against such horrible anomalies would have been great as this can be interpreted in quite a few ways. Some of which will just be seen as another proof of how horrible Garou as a whole are.<br /> <br /> The third is the letter of a wife to her husband, a Garou. It speaks of how she and her child were assaulted by strange assailants in the night, and even though she doesn't remember what happened, it's clear her child shifted and tore apart/drove away the attackers. The mother decides to take away the child and go far from the husband as possible, but it's clear that will not end well considering she now has a Garou on her hands. It's good, solid writing, and something I can see being a thing for many Garou who have to leave their families behind.<br /> <br /> The final section, Memory, left me very confused. The core story itself is strong - it speaks of inter-garou conflict, it speaks of attempts to cure fomori (tying into the Theurge section) and how things like these can be an excuse for Garou to murder other Garou over prejudice and fake allegations of corruption. It's told from the perspective of the last standing member of a pack that got wiped out, remembering their packmates and honouring their memory by being the lone guardian of their tale and their Caern, which will now be dedicated in the name of the fallen. The twist at the end if that the story is being told to the Garou who led the attack on the Caern, just before they kill them.<br /> <br /> Ok. That doesn't sound that weird. But the details are weird. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It's a Caern somewhere near Providence where Mother Larissa went to die. Wait. What? When? How? We just saw her in last chapter being her usual self? I cannot imagine her dying anywhere but in the Sept of Green, she is deeply, deeply tied to this place</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The person retelling this tale seems to have a male homid body and a female lupus body. I don't think I've ever seen something like that before. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The child they cured from the horrifying bane has done a lot of horrible things and most likely remembers them wakes up happy and overjoyed to be saved.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And the person the story is being told to has come here without their pack to be torn apart by the narrator. Now this is probably the weirdest bit as everything that follows will be a shitstorm. If they killed the pack leader, the rest of the pack is coming back and a lone Garou won't take them. Worse yet, it's a lone Garou defending a Caern that is known to be without defenders, more Garou are definitely coming to take over. This is framed into being somehow backed by the Margrave, the resident ominous Garou leader</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But what the hell does the Margrave even have to do with the Septs on the East coast of the U.S. ? The dude operates in Europe and that's his power base, this ties again into my rant about how people seem to miss the bigger picture and the geography in Werewolf for the big characters</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monkeywrenching</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The weird choices of how parts of the text are organised vex me here quite a bit. There is a strong theme of Monkeywrenching and different approaches and infodumps on how Pentex and its members operate, however it got split up with a number of other things happening in the chapter that are not thematically related to them. The last section is also spread through the book, but the chunks are so much more self contained. I'll try and list them out here as it's going to be easier to process them in context</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intercepted board meeting of Endron - a transcript with a lot of backstabbing, manipulation and casual employee murder</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Outlook Post #7 - a transcript of a soldier manning an outpost in the jungle noticing way too strange things going on - I loved this bit and it was some excellent world building and paranoia and typical Pentex Callousness</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Head Falls, Another Rises - The confession of the JFK Bomber Ragabash above and how he aimed to kill Ian Robertson, one of the up and coming Pentex directors as well as a news article about the event and how essentially it changed nothing in the bigger picture</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A recounting how a Sept in Virginia turned the Skull Pigs against Mike Dragon's-Wrath and used them to distract and hurt him enough to take him out</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A detailed report on monkey wrenching in action at GRC Consultants - support abuse, grassroots pressure, driving people in charge crazy, organising the staff...</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pentex has issued Kill Orders for a number of senior personnel to First Teams - can the Garou utilise this (intriguing plothook, wish there was a bit more detail)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All in all Three dead Pentex Directors in one chapter, and only one of them killed by a Garou being an idiot.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Inheritors</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I'm calling this section like this because it deals with a theme of what the world is like in the absence of the Lost Tribes and Breeds, and what some may think it will lead to. The first of the tales in this section is about the &quot;anti-dingo enthusiasts&quot; of the Outback, and how the local Garou hunt them down while avoiding the dissaproval of the local spirits. We get a glimpse into the Dreamtime and how strange it is compared to the usual Umbra and how its populated by strange and intriguing giant beasts. Just made me feel like I'd have loved to have seen a proper Rage Across Australia.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Kinfolk doctor is exploring where the shifters came from, and how certain breeds and tribes have changed their biology to suit other animals. She postulates that the Rite of Skin Walking and Minotaur may be something related to the Apis. Finally, she seeks out the Gumagan so that she may learn the rites that allow people to change their animal forms to help her own Tribe adapt to the coming world. Short, sweet, loaded with ideas and potential.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We learn of the Crow-Biting-Ferals, a pack that had a silly Kinfolk bagged and tagged by some weird biotech company after they submitted their DNA Ancestry Kit. Only to realise that there are horrors in there and that the company seeks to make strange hybrids and utilise the harvested DNA to create mockeries. I love this little vignette for the simple reason that it's pretty much an adventure of its own</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And then comes Glen-Seize-Trouble. Now Glen-Seize-Trouble is a posterboy for being too clever for his own good. He has this theory... that the Mockery breeds are not really the servitors of the Wyrm, but actually Pentex rediscovering the lost breeds and doing Gaia's work for her. He believes them to be Gaia's Backup plan. And his story continues by him travelling to Mozambique seeking to meet with what he believes to be a Yeren. He ropes in some local Glass Walkers to help him out, and they meet Jeremiah God-Buyer, the slickest, skeeviest used car salesman in all of Africa. And Jeremiah proceeds to provoke the Walkers and murder them with his security team which included nigh-unkillable Kerasi. We also get our first illustration of the Kerasi, but it's sadly 4 pages further\u200b! An interesting feature of the Yeren is that he did all this in plain sight, and managed to easily control the witnesses and the police into submission.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This leads Glen down a doom spiral in which he believes that his theses are wrong, and that the Wyrm has won. I believe that what follows is an episode of Harano, and its a harrowing experience for Glen, one in which he is not only confronted by his errors, but also with the errors of the Garou as a whole and how they must do better. His next step seems to be taking out one of the Pentex Directors (Pochard), so that does seem like he got better.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's not just the new breeds or the Garou having to pick up where the Bunyip were, because they also inherited some additional problems. We learn how <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Totem\" target=\"_blank\">Operation Totem</a> unleashed strange things from under the earth, and how the Bunyip, just like the Older Brother kept horrible things underground. And the most horrible of them is about to wake, and no-one knows how to put it back to sleep. Interestingly, it implies that &quot;his Tribe grows stronger&quot;. I'm not sure if this is a BSD totem or something entirely else?</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Tricksters</b><br /> This includes probably two of my favourite parts of the Ragabash tales. The first one is written from the perspective of two Black Spirals on a grisly mission to murder some Kinfolk who the spirits say may become Garou. They are as disgusting as should be expected, one of them looking forward to do horrible things to the girl, to which the other just says that they should do it when she's dead. Peak BSD. But the cool thing about the story is that they're walking into a trap, and using misdirection and trickery a Ragabash and a Theurge play them against each other and manage to get them to murder each other. It's brilliant and I'd love to see something like that pulled off in a game.<br /> <br /> Also, one of the BSD's is called Bleeds-The-Night. I found this hilarious as there is also a Rokea called &quot;Bleeds Night&quot;. Not going to cause confusion ever. Nope.<br /> <br /> The second tale is about Raccoon being interviewed by a young Ragabash looking for Wisdom. And Raccoon is being a total loonie here. His tone and way he communicates are priceless and he may be my favourite spirit in the book. He tells the Ragabash a tale about the Atahasia (the hidden metis Ananasi) rising up from giant cracks in the Earth and overtaking the city of Seattle, murdering most of downtown and setting up residence in one of the skyscrapers. There is of course a question if this tale is true, will be true and was ever true by the narrator, but the Raccoon tells him the tales are here to educate people (I do like the scene itself, even if doing it in Seattle would probably be an almost Apocalypse level scenario). The whole point of the tale is to speak of how Garou do war, with a Ragabash who brings news to a haughty Ahroun only to be executed, and how another clever Ragabash rather lets the Ahroun get killed and saves the rest of the Garou from dying like fools. It's a great one, it's educational, it criticizes certain Garou tendencies.<br /> <br /> ... and it's all an elaborate con by Old Man Manyskins who (as Raccoon) uses it to not just teach the young one a lesson that needs to be learned, but also point him towards looking for Turtle - another thread pointing toward the return of the Totem of the Croatan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Fate of House Blood Red Crest</b><br /> Aaand Pattern Recognition is back. And demonstrating their brilliant diplomatic acumen by sending over one of their Geomids to talk to a certain lupus Garou in the middle of Tibet. That, of course, doesn't end well. Thankfully, they manage to convince Nightmane, the Theurge of the Silver Fangs to take them from the Shigalu monastery into India and into the courts of House Blood Red Crest. They make an excellent argument that one of the best ways for Garou to understand each other is to tell tales of different experiences and different rulers.<br /> <br /> They travel from Shigalu with Nightmane into Khasi Hills, the domain of King Nayar of House Blood Red Crest. We see the local Garou participating in a festival, one of their Ragabash blessing marital unions, and ultimately King Nayar presenting his solution to the lack of new Garou being born to the house - they shall take any and all Crinos-born under their wing for the glory of the House and Falcon!<br /> <br /> It's a strong statement and one that makes sense. I liked Nightmane as a very sensible sort and Dalaja of the House Blood Red Crest sounded like a fun character. Hope we'll see more about her and the king in the pending Icons of Rage. I was sorry not to see details about the other parts of House Blood Red Crest that operate further to the East or any of their interactions with the local Hengeyokai, as in my games the House has to have extensive dealings with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Plot Hooks</span></span></b><br /> <br /> This may be the least interesting plothook section of the book so far. I've had better hooks in the text before it that were not even touched upon in the summary in the back.I'd probably single out the story seed where certain elements of the Silver Fangs see the choice of House Blood Red Crest as shameful and seeks to sabotage or destroy them, and places the PC's between the two sides. This one has the makings of a solid chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T20:20:36-07:00","id":1523938,"title":"","content":"Just fyi, when written, the &quot;Family Sickness&quot; is in fact the same family as &quot;Free-X&quot;/&quot;Freaks&quot;. The daughter's name is the key there. So that Ragabash attended the birthday, but when he says he shouldn't have returned, it's in light of the Free-X events. Not exactly premeditated slaughter of three generations of Kinfolk. Not much better, in terms of outcome, mind you. Nan is old, Rowan has lost his parents and sister.<br /> <br /> I wonder what becomes of an orphaned Kinfolk child?<br /> <br /> I'd like to point out that Jasmine's scream was supernatural. The tale teller isn't lying when he says her scream literally burst his ear drums. I took that power from Freak Legion. It's subtle, until used. Jasmine didn't know she had this devastating power, or maybe she did and she was being groomed as a &quot;Black Canary&quot; equivalent? Regardless, it's not something that Ragabash was expecting, and that's where he went wrong, really. He didn't look hard enough, or investigate long enough to realize she was already a Fomori, and was caught by surprise by a power his niece didn't understand, that caused injury and Frenzy-with-a-capital-F - even in an Auspice with the least starting Rage. If only he had Sense Wyrm? Or, given the status of the house per Family Sickness, would that even have worked? And she may have had some other power that alerted her to the Ragabash's presence beside her bed - or maybe he was a bit too confident sneaking around and failed a stealth roll? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, it was supposed to be a tragic and cautionary tale - even the supposedly cleverest and least Rage filled Garou have blind spots, make mistakes, fall prey to Frenzy and the Wyrm Urges within their hearts.<br /> <br /> Those tales were meant to lead into the Crow-Biting-Ferals raid. Again, the names should link them, however I'm aware that the order in the final book makes it a bit trickier to follow.<br /> <br /> And the CBFs are Glen's pack. And they get frustrated with him when Ben Spears-the-Web conveys the Jeremiah God-Buyer incident. Because just maybe two extra Garou could've turned the fight? But the Ragabash pack leader held himself and Ben back. oh look, trying to be clever and cautious probably saved their lives but maybe, just maybe, they would've been victorious? But also, the Kerasi and Yeren were unexpected. And powerful. And the Yeren's Gift for dodging blame/responsibility is quite incredible. And utterly terrifying for Glen who's maybe done some bad things in his life and been rightly punished (or corrected, or disciplined) and (hopefully) learned from his misdeeds however much he regrets them - yet this Yeren guy just calls on a magic trick to avoid all that?! No responsibility, no accountability - do whatever you want and pin it on someone else to suffer consequences. Glen's working through the implications, you just don't get that depth in such a short tale.<br /> <br /> Poor Glen. Falling deep into Harano and still desperately trying to fight the Wyrm until he goes somewhere that just maybe he shouldn't... but I don't think you've hit that connection yet so #Spoilers!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T04:40:37-07:00","id":1524058,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"167\" data-vbnamecard=\"167\">nikink</a> Thanks for pitching in and clarifying this. I honestly had to go back to the book to actually realise that these two are the same after you said this. With both stories being presented in first perspective, I read them as two different accounts, grouped together for their similarity. It didn't help that the second account spoke less of the reason why the narrator went back and it really could be read as &quot;I went back to kill them because they disgusted me&quot;. Especially as it feeled to me that Nan's birthday was the inciting incident, not Jasmine going crazy on the narrator. And unlike some of the other characters in this section, at least this character is wracked with guilt and feels they messed up. I don't think the way they are laid out is helping this.<br /> <br /> I caught the reference to the Roar of the Wyrm and Jasmine triggering the frenzy. Mind you, I've never been of the school of thought that Rage comes from the Wyrm. It feels like the Garou should be responsible for their own failings, and when they make the Wyrm stronger it should be because they fucked up, not because of an inherent trait of theirs.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I was compltley oblivious to the fact that CBF's or Glen are connected in any way. I assume the letter detailing the incursion is penned by Glen? A signature would have done wonders there.Spears the Web was the guy I connected with Glen and Glen's quest, and he is not mentioned in the letter. I did like Glen, even if I felt he was a nuts. The thing with him is that he's another cautionary tale, and it seems that a lot of this chapter is just cautionary tales.<br /> <br /> Do you, possibly, have any idea what the context of the &quot;Your War&quot; sidebar is? I was unsure if that was supposed to be tied into the narrator of the Family Sickness tale or just a tale of kinfolk/hunters meeting out justice to horrible Garou (as in the secret society)?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T03:45:19-07:00","id":1524090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518531-wir-the-apocalyptic-record?p=1524058#post1524058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"167\" data-vbnamecard=\"167\">nikink</a> Thanks for pitching in and clarifying this. I honestly had to go back to the book to actually realise that these two are the same after you said this. With both stories being presented in first perspective, I read them as two different accounts, grouped together for their similarity. It didn't help that the second account spoke less of the reason why the narrator went back and it really could be read as &quot;I went back to kill them because they disgusted me&quot;. Especially as it feeled to me that Nan's birthday was the inciting incident, not Jasmine going crazy on the narrator. And unlike some of the other characters in this section, at least this character is wracked with guilt and feels they messed up. I don't think the way they are laid out is helping this.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. Despite what I may have intended, things change through development. Death of the author kicks in. Doesn't matter what I may have meant, only what's present in the final product. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I caught the reference to the Roar of the Wyrm and Jasmine triggering the frenzy. Mind you, I've never been of the school of thought that Rage comes from the Wyrm. It feels like the Garou should be responsible for their own failings, and when they make the Wyrm stronger it should be because they fucked up, not because of an inherent trait of theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. But Fomori powers that trigger frenzy, trigger frenzy. FWIW I think there's another part in the book - coming next I think? - where the Garou speaking says outright that the Garou are responsible for their actions, Rage or no, because it's all too easy to blame your Rage for doing whatever you wanted to do after the fact. For what it's worth, I'm pretty sure Glenn would agree with that stance.<br /> <br /> So Glenn doesn't blame anyone else for his errors here. He killed his family - not the Wyrm, not pollution, not Pentex, not Jasmine; It's on him. After all, he's a Ragabash, he should've put more thought and cleverness into this situation. Unfortunately such an ideal isn't always observed in practice. Especially when the stakes are personal where it's so easy for judgment to be clouded by love and familiarity. If Glenn had been wiser he'd've delegated the investigation to someone else - perhaps in his own pack, if possible another pack altogether. In an alternate timeline where the War of Rage hadn't happened, this sort of investigation would've been the sort of thing a Bastet was ideal for, imo. C'est la vie.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand I was compltley oblivious to the fact that CBF's or Glen are connected in any way. I assume the letter detailing the incursion is penned by Glen? A signature would have done wonders there.Spears the Web was the guy I connected with Glen and Glen's quest, and he is not mentioned in the letter. I did like Glen, even if I felt he was a nuts. The thing with him is that he's another cautionary tale, and it seems that a lot of this chapter is just cautionary tales.</div> </div> </div> </div>All fair. See above for changes between what I may have had in mind and the final product. The connections may become more obvious later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you, possibly, have any idea what the context of the &quot;Your War&quot; sidebar is? I was unsure if that was supposed to be tied into the narrator of the Family Sickness tale or just a tale of kinfolk/hunters meeting out justice to horrible Garou (as in the secret society)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Afraid not - I didn't write it. I would lean towards the latter opinion myself - kinfolk hunter taking revenge on a Garou who appears to have tried to blame their Rage on the violence they committed.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}